  "proof_topology": [
    "Assume a nonzero-offset P8 point on Q6=0 and D(H2*Delta).",
    "The six GLD101 selectors are among P8, so the exact GLD101 determinant/norm bridge forces one of the eight norm-support factors.",
    "If B=0 then C!=0 and the arbitrary-p generic C-open certificate is contradictory.",
    "If B!=0 then C=B*t and common-B cancellation is reversible.",
    "The p and p-1 supports are closed at a=0 by the exact GLD102 selected-minor subcases; p^2+1, R4, R8, and R110 are closed by their respective B-open leaves.",
    "The P support lies on Delta=0 and the H2 support lies outside D(H2), so neither is silently claimed closed.",
    "Every support case is therefore impossible at a nonzero offset, proving the P8 implication; rank(M)<=6 supplies P8 only in the forward direction."
  ],
